course: dictionary
lesson: 6582
title: Ninth: place and part
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Ninth» is a number word for place in order. It comes after eighth, so it is number 9 in the line-up. It is written 9th.
explain: The same word can also mean a part. A ninth is one of nine equal parts of something, which we write as 1/9. Cut a cake into nine equal slices and each slice is a ninth.
explain: Look at the words around it. «Great Britain is the largest island in Europe and the ninth largest in the world.» The clue is largest in the world, so ninth is a place in order, not a piece. Ask: is this about order, or about sharing into equal parts?
fact: Ninth means number 9 in order, and it is written 9th.
fact: A ninth is one of nine equal parts, written as 1/9.
fact: In music, a ninth is a gap of nine notes.
fact: «Ninth grade» is a school year in the USA and Canada.
fact: In the old Roman calendar, «November (nov = 9) the ninth» was the ninth month of the year.
exercise: «Great Britain is the largest island in Europe and the ninth largest in the world.» What does ninth tell you here? | It is a musical note | It is one of nine equal parts | It is the biggest of all | *Its place in order is number 9
exercise: What is a ninth of a pizza? | Nine slices | One half of the pizza | Nine times as big as the pizza | *One of nine equal parts
exercise: In the old Roman calendar, which month was the ninth month? | December | September | October | *November
test: «The ninth day of the trip was the best.» Which day is this? | 6th | *9th | 10th | 1st
test: What is the word for 1/9? | A nine | A nineteen | *A ninth | A ninety
exam: «The ninth day of the trip was the best.» What does ninth tell you? | How many friends came along | How many days the trip lasted | The name of a food | *Which day it is in order
